+  Recognition trust model: a match is a cosine score at or above
+  ADA_SPEAKER_THRESHOLD (default 0.45) with a 0.05 margin over the
+  runner-up — a voiceprint, not proof of identity. A similar-sounding
+  voice or a replayed recording can cross it, so treat the name as
+  strong evidence, not authentication. The owner-tier rule: a speaker
+  whose person policy is full-access (person.tony) keeps owner rights
+  when recognized on ANY lane — including a member lane keyed to
+  someone else — which is why the threshold+margin exist; do NOT widen
+  that rule to 'best score wins'. The [voice: speaker=..] context on
